            <div class="space-y-4 text-slate-700 text-[16px]">
              <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 space-y-2">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-lg">Ben Dinh Sector (Nhuan Duc Commune)</h3>
                <ul class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
                  <li><strong>Location:</strong> Roughly 50 km northwest of District 1 (about 1.5 to 2 hours drive).</li>
                  <li><strong>Wartime Role:</strong> Headquarters of the Cu Chi District Party Committee.</li>
                  <li><strong>Atmosphere:</strong> Ben Dinh handles the vast majority of commercial day-tour buses because it's closer to the city with wide access roads and large parking bays. It has large orientation pavilions, wide paved walkways, and busy souvenir stalls.</li>
                  <li><strong>The Tunnels:</strong> Passages here are heavily widened, fitted with concrete safety collars, and lit throughout.</li>
                  <li><strong>Best For:</strong> Travelers on tight schedules, families wanting shorter driving times, and standard half-day morning tours.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-amber-50/60 border border-amber-200 space-y-2">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-900 text-lg">Ben Duoc Sector (Phu My Hung Commune)</h3>
                <ul class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
                  <li><strong>Location:</strong> Roughly 65 to 70 km northwest of District 1 (about 2 to 2.5 hours drive).</li>
                  <li><strong>Wartime Role:</strong> Command headquarters for the Saigon–Gia Dinh Military Zone and Regional Party Committee (<em>Khu ủy Sài Gòn - Chợ Lớn - Gia Định</em>).</li>
                  <li><strong>Atmosphere:</strong> Set among peaceful rubber tree plantations and native forest along the Saigon River, Ben Duoc sees far fewer large tour coaches. The atmosphere is quiet, unhurried, and noticeably more reflective.</li>
                  <li><strong>Key Landmark:</strong> The monumental <strong>Ben Duoc Martyrs Memorial Temple</strong> (<em>Đền Bến Dược</em>), a 7-hectare commemorative sanctuary honoring 44,752 fallen heroes, martyrs, and Vietnamese Heroic Mothers inscribed on stone steles.</li>
                  <li><strong>The Tunnels:</strong> Offers a more authentic feeling, including multiple depth levels alongside reinforced visitor paths.</li>
                  <li><strong>Best For:</strong> History enthusiasts, photographers, independent travelers, and anyone exploring by private car who prefers quiet woodland over tourist crowds.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
