                  <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Smokeless Kitchen & Cassava Tasting</div>
                  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-0.5">Stop at a reconstructed Hoàng Cầm kitchen to see the underground smoke-dispersion vents, then sit down for hot boiled cassava dipped in crushed roasted peanuts, sugar, and salt (<em>khoai mì chấm muối mè</em>) with hot tea.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs shrink-0 mt-0.5">8</span>
                <div>
                  <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Optional Shooting Range</div>
                  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-0.5">On the outer perimeter, the National Defense Sports Shooting Range allows visitors over 18 to fire historic military rifles under military supervision. <strong>Good to know:</strong> Gunfire from the range echoes through the woods and is clearly audible along the walking trails. If you're expecting dead quiet, the sudden crack of rifle fire can catch you off guard.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
