                  width="1280"
                  height="720"
                  loading="lazy"
                />
              </div>
              <p class="text-center text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-500 italic mt-2.5">
                Travelers exploring shaded walking paths under the regenerated forest canopy at Cu Chi.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-4 text-slate-700 text-[16px]">
              <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
                <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">1. Private Car Transfer (Most Flexible & Comfortable)</div>
                <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
                  Transit Time: 1.5 to 2 hours each way (~$65 to $95 USD for a private SUV or van). Door-to-door hotel pickup, climate control, flexible departure times, and the freedom to choose Ben Duoc over Ben Dinh. Read our complete guide: <a href="/visiting-cu-chi-tunnels-by-private-car" class="text-amber-800 hover:underline font-semibold">Visiting Cu Chi Tunnels by Private Car</a>.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
                <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">2. Guided Small-Group or Private Tour</div>
                <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
                  Cost: ~$35 to $60 USD for minivans; ~$85 to $130 USD per person for private tours. Includes a licensed English-speaking guide, air-conditioned transport, entrance tickets, and bottled water. A knowledgeable guide translates the earthen pits into living history. Read: <a href="/is-a-cu-chi-tunnels-private-tour-worth" class="text-amber-800 hover:underline font-semibold">Is a Cu Chi Tunnels Private Tour Worth the Extra Cost?</a>
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
                <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">3. Luxury Speedboat Excursion</div>
                <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
                  Transit Time: ~75 to 90 minutes each way along the Saigon River (~$85 to $120 USD). Bypasses highway traffic entirely and offers scenic riverbank views as urban Saigon gives way to rural fruit orchards. Most speedboats dock directly at Ben Dinh.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
                <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">4. Public Bus (Budget Backpacker Route)</div>
                <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
                  Transit Time: 2.5 to 3.5 hours each way (~$1.50 to $2 USD). Bus #13 from 23/9 Park to Cu Chi Bus Station, then transfer to Bus #79 for Ben Duoc or Bus #63 for Ben Dinh. Keep in mind: buses are not air-conditioned to Western standards and require multiple stops and transfers.
                </p>
              </div>
